@page "/privacy"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy</PageTitle>

<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="text-muted">Last updated: 2026-09-17</p>

<p>
    Workplace is a personal tool built and used by a single person (Johan Olsson) to view calendar
    events from connected Google and Microsoft calendars and assign a work location to each day.
    It is not a public product, and access to it is restricted to its one owner.
</p>

<h2>Data we access</h2>
<p>
    When you connect a Google or Microsoft calendar, the app requests read-only access
    (read-write only for a personal Microsoft calendar you connect for scheduling) and uses it to
    fetch each event's title, start time, end time, and whether it's an all-day event. It does not
    read attendees, descriptions, locations, or attachments.
</p>

<h2>Data we store</h2>
<p>
    The app stores, in a local database on the server it runs on:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>OAuth access and refresh tokens for each connected account, encrypted at rest</li>
    <li>The list of connected accounts, along with the display name and colour you assign them</li>
    <li>A snapshot of your work calendar, synced from a desktop Outlook client for the work-tenant leg</li>
    <li>The work-location assignments you make for each day in the app</li>
</ul>

<h2>What we don't do</h2>
<p>
    There is no analytics or tracking, no advertising, and no sale or sharing of your data with
    third parties. Calendar data is used only to display your own agenda back to you.
</p>

<h2>Retention and control</h2>
<p>
    You can disconnect any calendar at any time from the <a href="connections">Connections</a> page,
    which removes its stored tokens. You can also revoke the app's access at any time from your
    Google Account or Microsoft Account permissions settings.
</p>

<h2>Access restriction</h2>
<p>
    Signing in to the app itself is restricted to a single allowed account, so even though the app
    is reachable on the internet, nobody else can sign in or see this data.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
    Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:johan.olsson@thetribe.tech">johan.olsson@thetribe.tech</a>.
</p>
